  "body": "This change updates some examples of `<pre>` elements to not use `<code>` children, and also updates some related non-normative guidance in the spec to advise that when marking up `<pre>` elements that contain content written in particular programming language, a class attribute+value on the `<pre>` element itself can be used to indicate the language — without the need to always instead add a `<code>` child with a class attribute+value.\n\nRelates to https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/3764\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/3772/grouping-content.html\" title=\"Last updated on Jun 24, 2018, 11:27 PM GMT (896fb83)\">/grouping-content.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/3772/78741b7...896fb83/grouping-content.html\" title=\"Last updated on Jun 24, 2018, 11:27 PM GMT (896fb83)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/3772/text-level-semantics.html\" title=\"Last updated on Jun 24, 2018, 11:27 PM GMT (896fb83)\">/text-level-semantics.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/3772/78741b7...896fb83/text-level-semantics.html\" title=\"Last updated on Jun 24, 2018, 11:27 PM GMT (896fb83)\">diff</a> )",
